<header><h1>💾 Data Backup Guide</h1><p>Keep your important digital work safe.</p></header>
<main>
<section class="card"><h2>What Is a Backup?</h2><p>A backup is an extra copy of your files that can help you recover them if the originals are lost or damaged.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Backup Options</h2><ul><li>External hard drive or USB storage</li><li>Trusted cloud storage</li><li>A separate computer or storage device</li></ul></section>
<section class="card"><h2>The 3-2-1 Rule</h2><p>Keep 3 copies of important data, on 2 different types of storage, with 1 copy stored off-site.</p><p>This is a useful guideline for important files, not a guarantee against every risk.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>What Should Students Back Up?</h2><ul><li>College assignments</li><li>HTML and programming projects</li><li>Presentation slides</li><li>Practical notes and reports</li></ul></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Good Backup Habits</h2><p class="tip">✓ Back up regularly.<br>✓ Keep copies separate from your main device.<br>✓ Protect cloud accounts with strong security.<br>✓ Test occasionally that your files can be restored.</p></section>
</main>
